@startuml ws-separation-flow
title WebSocket Separation — Layer Ownership (CP7f actual)

skinparam backgroundColor #eaedf1
skinparam sequenceArrowColor #3b82f6
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #3b82f6
skinparam participantBorderColor #1e2d3d
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #0d1117
skinparam participantFontColor #f1f5f9
skinparam noteBorderColor #1e2d3d
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #0f1623
skinparam noteFontColor #9ca3af

participant "MapWidget" as UI
participant "useLiveFeed()\nfeatures/live-feed" as Hook
participant "openWebSocket()\nshared/realtime" as Client
participant "WebSocket\n(browser)" as WS
participant "API WS Server" as API

== Mount ==

UI -> Hook : useLiveFeed({ onPositionUpdate, onDemoExpired })
note over Hook
  Hook opens WS immediately on mount.
  subscribe(bbox) is returned to MapWidget
  and called imperatively after map loads.
end note
Hook -> Client : openWebSocket(WS_URL, { onOpen, onMessage, onClose })
Client -> WS : new WebSocket(url)
WS -> API : HTTP upgrade + sentinel_jwt cookie
API -> WS : 101 Switching Protocols
Client -> Hook : onOpen callback — sets sendRef.current

== REST hydration + subscribe ==

note over UI
  map.on('load') fires.
  MapWidget fetches GET /entities/live?bbox=...
  and seeds entities Map from the REST response.
  Then calls subscribe(viewBbox).
end note
UI -> Hook : subscribe([minLat, minLon, maxLat, maxLon])
Hook -> Client : sendRef.current(JSON)
Client -> WS : ws.send({ type: "subscribe", bbox })
WS -> API : subscribe message

note over API
  Server stores bbox per connection.
  Filters position-updates to bbox.
  Sends all alert-events (no bbox filter).
end note

== Live position updates ==

API -> WS : { channel: "position-updates", data: { entity_id, timestamp_ms, lat, lon, ... } }
WS -> Client : onmessage event
Client -> Hook : onMessage(raw string)
Hook -> Hook : JSON.parse — parsePositionFrame(data)
note right of Hook
  Validates entity_id, lat, lon, timestamp_ms.
  Returns null on malformed frame — React state
  is never touched.
  timestamp_ms maps to eventTimeMs.
  entity_subtype and on_ground are null
  (not present in WS update wire format).
end note
Hook -> UI : onPositionUpdate(entity)
UI -> UI : setEntities(applyPositionUpdate(prev, entity))
note right of UI
  applyPositionUpdate discards the frame if
  incoming.eventTimeMs <= stored.eventTimeMs
  (monotonicity guard against stale frames).
end note

== Unexpected close (reconnect) ==

WS -> Client : onclose (code != 4401)
Client -> Hook : onClose(code)
Hook -> Hook : sendRef.current = null
Hook -> Hook : setTimeout 5 s
Hook -> Client : openWebSocket(...) — new connection
note right of Hook
  Closure variable 'stopped' guards against
  reconnect after unmount.
  No REST re-hydration on reconnect in CP7f —
  WS updates resume and fill the entity map.
end note

== Demo expiry (no reconnect) ==

WS -> Client : onclose (code 4401)
Client -> Hook : onClose(4401)
Hook -> Hook : sendRef.current = null
Hook -> UI : onDemoExpired()
UI -> UI : setDemoExpired(true) — render DemoExpiredBanner
note right of UI
  onDemoExpired is threaded from DashboardPage
  via Workspace props to MapWidget params
  to useLiveFeed option.
end note

== Unmount cleanup ==

UI -> Hook : component unmount (useEffect cleanup)
Hook -> Hook : stopped = true
Hook -> Hook : clearTimeout(reconnectTimer)
Hook -> Client : activeClose() — ws.close()
Client -> WS : close()

@enduml
